    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d942">

                <pb facs="0845" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3004.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Mexican Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to our
                    conversation on the 28th instant, when you again urged that this Government take
                    some drastic action in relation to Mr. Vasquez<anchor n="1" xml:id="d942-f1"/>
                    at San Antonio, Texas, it is my duty to inform your excellency that, although
                    the greatest circumspection is being exercised, there has not, up to the present
                    time, been proven on the part of Mr. Vásquez any act which falls within the
                    statutes of the United States.</p>
                <p>I may remark that your excellency will gain a clear idea as to the legal aspects
                    of such cases by referring to the correspondence of the Department with your
                    Embassy during the Madero revolution; for example, the letter of December 1,
                        1910,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d942-f2"/> aide-mémoire of January 23,
                        1911,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d942-f3"/> and the letter of June 7, 1911.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d942-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
